4 When you should NOT use zeolite in your aquarium
The structure is completed with several parts that contain some pores of greater diameter. It is really that ion exchange capacity that enables the absorption of the polluting elements present in the water and the possible filtration.
We remember that it is a substrate capable of exchanging ammonia and that it works differently in fresh or salt water. It is important to know the function of zeolite depending on the type of aquarium that we are going to have.
Zeolite is not infinite, but it degrades over time and loses its effectiveness. This is because the bacterial colonies are reproducing to the point of clogging the pores on the surface.
When zeolite is used in an aquarium to aid in filtration It is recommended to use gradually. That is, you should never start filtering the water with all the zeolite loads.
When you should NOT use zeolite in your aquarium
Many aquarium experts agree on the great contribution that this material has in a newly created aquarium. However, even in new aquariums, the addition of ammonia to the medium causes the zeolite to have to act as a short-term base.
It is important to avoid the problems that it can generate due to its great capacity for molecular exchange. For it, we must install it little by little over several weeks.
