Over the years a false myth has been created in which it is believed that fish have a bad memory, but in reality it is not like that, different studies show the opposite. Today we will refer to an Australian investigation in which it is recognized that fish have very good memories.
Most fish have a great ability to remember their predators up to almost a year later of being attacked by them. For example, a carp that has been about to bite the hook remembers the experience and avoids the weighers for several months.
In this way, it was confirmed that fish have long-term memory, in addition to learning to know their habitat in depth and associate the abundance of food or the dangers found in certain places.
