If the operation is correct, it is safe for fish and microorganisms and will not produce any kind of side effects. It is recommended to use it in the morning, after a partial water change of at least 30%, when the product is in a good oxygen concentration.
It has a liquid format so that it can be distributed well throughout the aquarium and reached every corner. However, we must continue to control very well all the variables within the aquarium so that the proliferation of algae can be permanently stopped.
The first thing to do is use the proper aquarium tests to have a good regular check of the water quality. Regularly, the aquarium forces us to carry out maintenance tasks, such as partial water changes to eliminate some of the nitrates that cannot be eliminated by the aquarium's filtration system: plants, substrates, filters, etc.
It is relatively easy for algae to appear in an aquarium if conditions are not stable. Normally it is usually due to an excess of light in the location where the aquarium was located, due to excess nitrates or phosphates for the fertilizers used in the plants.
The anti-algae used in the aquarium are chemical products that can prevent and eliminate the appearance of algae, quickly inhibit its growth, and do not harm other residents of the aquarium such as plants, fish, mollusks and any microorganism. They are usually used in a liquid format so that it can reach all the corners of the aquarium and act as quickly as possible.
One of the ways to do a homemade anti-algae is to use straw. The straw stains the water a light amber color and does not allow light to penetrate, which favors the growth of algae.
These types of products abound in the market and there are many types to choose from. Let's summarize which are the best anti-algae for aquariums:
Easy Life anti-algae: This brand has two different products for the action of green algae and for blue algae and cyanobacteria. Therefore, depending on the problem you have in your aquarium, you can use one product or another.
