2 What is gravel used for in an aquarium?
It is a type of white gravel for aquariums that is considered to be of a medium grain size. It serves as a natural substrate to adapt aquariums in a way that resembles a natural environment as much as possible.
It is a type of white gravel for aquariums that is mainly used to decorate and help in the cleaning of natural aquariums. It is not toxic and does not release carbonates in use.
