How many days can a fish go without eating?
There are times when we can hear how it is stated outright that fish can go up to almost a week without eating. Such a feat may come to pass, but it is certainly difficult, so I advise you not to trust it.
In the first place, if the fish are hungry we can observe how their behavior is more restless than usual, they climb several times to the upper areas of the water looking for some food. Ultimately, they become anxious.
Finally, it should be noted that when food is scarce or null, fish can go through processes of such anxiety, which forces and drives them to engage in a behavior that borders on cannibalism, since in their incessant search for food they will be able to attack and kill other individuals. So, if we see several fish in our aquarium with wounds on their fins and tail or fish that have disappeared suspiciously, it is a sign that something is not going very well.
Actually, there are few tricks that exist to make our fish last as long as possible without eating, since the lack of food causes the animal to not be able to continue with its vital processes correctly and to enter into serious danger. Therefore, the most effective thing is to try to prevent our fish from going through long periods of famine, although it is true that sometimes unforeseen problems arise that make it impossible for us to supply them with food for some time.
I would also recommend you buy an automatic fish feeder. With this you will solve the problem in the vast majority of cases.
Unfortunately, there are many times when we have to leave home, for example on vacation, and we have no one to take care of and feed our animals.
There are some shells or tabletsThe most characteristic ones are whitish in color, which are arranged in the fish tanks and which dissolve little by little, releasing some substances that serve as food for the fish. It is true that we have to be especially careful with them, since some of the substances they release can alter the parameters of the water and cause the opposite effect to what we want.
