Which is better, aquarium sand or gravel?
Sand is more decorative than gravel but can become overly compacted. If we want to have an aquarium with real plants, it is better to use gravel so that the plants can develop better.
An easy way to calculate how much gravel you need in your aquarium is the following. Multiply the length by the width of the aquarium and by the number of centimeters thick you want to have gravel.
To wash the gravel from the aquarium you just need to place it in a large and clean sieve and pour water over it. Next we gently agitate and rinse the gravel over a bucket instead of the drain so that it can slide stably.
Within bony fish there is a great variety, and its main characteristic is that its skeleton is ossified, as we can see in the hippocampus or in seaweed fish. They have a mouth positioned at the end of their head and as for the fins we must say that they vary a lot, although most of them are completely atrophied.
All cartilaginous fish They have the characteristic of having a cartilage skeleton and generally most species have very sharp scales that can give the impression that they are teeth. Within this group we find sharks and rays, since we speak of one of the most predatory marine species that exist.
The fish are really the central and most important part of the aquarium, so we want them to stay in good condition and like any other inhabitant, they produce certain wastes that tend to dirty our pond. These wastes are basically ammonia and ammonia, while any other waste that falls to the bottom and is deposited on the substrate of the aquarium will decompose and produce greater amounts of ammonia.
Nitrites They are also toxic but nitrates are less toxic than these, so it is advisable to always have a colony of bacteria so that they can eliminate and decompose ammonia and ammonium into nitrites, which in turn will produce nitrates that will serve as fertilizer for the plants. .
Betta fish, everything you need to know about them
In this case, we talk about the Betta Fish. A fish well known for its bright and showy colors, known for being Siamese fighting fish and for the aggressiveness that the male has towards other betta fish.
They had their habitats in places like rice fields, ditches used for drainage, and in some ponds in the region's warm floodplains. These fish have suffered numerous storms, floods and devastating droughts and have been able to develop incredible adaptation mechanisms that they make them able to survive in almost any environment.
Although betta fish can survive in small spaces and in water that is not very good quality, they do best in small aquariums. In order for them to survive well and have a good quality of life, we must provide regular changes in the water.
Bettas have a turned mouth and normally feed on the surface of the water. Because they are able to breathe for short periods of time out of the water, they are not afraid of approaching the surface.
There is a myth that says that peace lilies or the roots of plants grown in the habitats of Betta fish can serve as food for them. But this is just a myth, since Bettas they cannot survive on plant roots.
They are different phenotypes of the same species. Some of the most appreciated types of betta splendens are:
Betta cooper fish is characterized by its special colors.
Betta dragon fish it is characterized by a special scale. Its scales are larger, especially they reflect light differently, emitting white-like flashes.
The male and the female must know each other, otherwise, if we put the female in without the male knowing her, he will treat her as an intruder and attack him. For this we must separate the aquarium by means of a plastic or glass so that they can be observed without touching.
Signs that tell us that something is wrong
If the pond temperature drops below 22 degrees or so, the fish will get sick. The best temperature is about 26 degrees so that they are more comfortable and a neutral or slightly acidic pH (6,5 at most).
The fish fighting problem starts when two males are placed in the same tank or when a beta male is in a community tank with other fish that are also aggressive. We also have to take into account that we should not keep betta fish with other colorful fish, since these can confuse it with other Bettas and attack them.
Bettas love having places to hide, especially females. For it we must implement a few hiding places to keep them happy.
Betta fry are sold for 1 euro. As you can see, these fish can be somewhat violent and fighting, but they are all wonderful and easy to care for.
