Perlon for aquarium, an essential material for your aquarium. | Of fishes
The perlon for aquarium is a material that you can use as a filter, with many advantages, and that can be of great help to keep the water in your aquarium clean whether you are an expert or if you have just adopted your first minnows.
6 Is it better perlon or sponge?
The greyhound is a synthetic fiber, very similar to cotton, which is used to use due to its extraordinary filtering power. Although it can be used for all types of filters, its use is wildly popular as an aquarium filter.
It's a highly elastic material, which fully adapts to your needs (although be careful not to stretch it too much or it will lose its filtering properties)
Post lasts a long time and it does not need constant maintenance.
How to put perlon in filter
The most important thing is that, when mounting the filtrate, first put the foamex sponge. This material is the first that must pass through the dirty water that comes from the aquarium, since, if it were mounted upside down, all the particles would try to pass through the perlon at the same time, which would "clog" it and cause the water not to leaked, which, on top of that, could alter the ecosystem in which your fish live.
How often do I have to change the perlon filter?
Often This change will depend on your aquarium, how often you clean the other sponge and the care you have with the greyhound: the change could be from a few weeks, to months to even a year.
You can, and in fact it is highly recommended because that way it is not necessary to be changing it every two by three. The only thing you should bear in mind is that you cannot wash the greyhound (or, by the way, the foamex sponge) with tap water, as this would unbalance the biological balance of the water in the tank.
For neither the one nor the other: the dog and the sponge must go together, since if you only put one separately, its function will not be correct. Thus, if we put only perlon, the dirt in the water will immediately plug the filter and it will not be able to absorb everything, which, of course, will influence the quality and transparency of the water in your aquarium.
The sponge, by the way, has to be made of foamex. It is not a very expensive material and can be washed, like the aquarium perlon, so it will last a long time.
Although at first glance they are so similar, They are very different materials, since the perlon, being synthetic, holds much better, lasts longer and does not fall apartUnlike cotton, which can make your water look like foxes.
However, we insist: better not to look for substitutes for the greyhound, a material that is already very cheap and fulfills its function perfectly.
The perlon is easy to use, it does not need excessive maintenance (although that depends on each one and your aquarium, of course), it is cheap and easy to clean. You just have to combine it with a sponge so that its filtration is correct, and make sure that it is not organic cotton so that it does not become clogged or degraded.
