This is of great help if in our aquarium we have natural algae that proliferate too quickly. With these fish we will help to control algae populations and have the aquarium a little better conditioned.
Catfish are distributed throughout the world except for Antarctica. At present it is estimated that the number of species far exceeds more than two thousand species.
Catfish usually spend most of their time in the bottom of the aquarium foraging for food. Almost all are nocturnal, although there are some groups, such as the locarids that are diurnal and are related to other fish such as corydoras.
In what comes to be the behavior of these fish with respect to others that you may have in the tank, you must bear in mind that catfish parasitize other fish (family Trichomycteridae).
When buying a catfish for your aquarium it is essential know the customs of the same to prepare the aquarium in one way or another. Keep in mind that habits vary greatly between each species.
For the bottom of the aquarium it is recommended that you have a fine structure so that they can adapt well to the background. We must remember that these fish spend most of their time at the bottom of the aquarium and, if we put fine structure such as gravel, they will adapt better and it will prevent tentacles from being injured.
The best catfish for your aquarium and price
If, on the other hand, you have a large aquarium, the best ones are the plecostomus, because they are larger and of spectacular beauty, although they are nocturnal. Their maintenance is easy and they are compatible with other fish in the aquarium.
To increase the color of your fish tank you can choose those of the Pseudopimelodidae family. They stand out for their orange and black stripes.
With this information you can properly take care of your catfish and have a fish tank full of curious species.
