These friendly animals have reached such popularity because, really, they do not require excessive care, however, you do have to pay special attention to certain details such as food. And it is that, How long can a fish go without eating?
4 How to prevent our fish from going without food?
Under normal conditions, a fish could go without food for about 2-3 days. Once this period has elapsed, the animal will show a certain weakness, which is logical on the one hand, and this lack of food and nutrients will cause the defenses to plummet considerably.
If you are going to be away for more than 2 or 3 days, a very useful solution is to bet on an automatic feeder, so the fish will not run out of food during the time we are absent.
If, for any reason, our fish has not eaten food for some time, it will show a series of symptoms that will serve as a warning sign to act as soon as possible.
This is followed by another series of symptoms that do not affect behavior so much, but rather act on the physical state of the animal and emerge when the famine process is really advanced. They are seen above all on your skin and scales, which lose brightness and color, sometimes presenting a rather deteriorated appearance..
Tips for a fish to go longer without eating
If such a case occurs, there are some guidelines or precautions that can help our fish survive a little longer. One of them is to provide our fish with a rich and varied diet at all times that allows them to have certain reserves of fat and energy, and that keeps them healthy and strong.
Other measures have to do, and a lot, with water.The water in our fish tanks, aquariums or ponds has to be as clean as possible. If we achieve this, we will make the habitat of our pets free of infections, bacteria and parasites that can play a trick on them if the fish are weak, as happens when they have not ingested anything for several hours.
How to prevent our fish from going without food?
