The Otocinclus is a very peaceful fish endemic to the southeast of Brazil, the Mato Grosso jungle and some rivers of Colombia, whose common name is the window cleaner. Do you want to know everything about this fish?
The waters where these fish live usually have rocks covered with algae and abundant vegetation.
Their feeding in the natural habitat is contingent on what they can uproot from the rocks and logs at the bottom, generally encrusting algae, small plants and microorganisms that live among them. They mainly have twilight habits, although they remain quite active during daylight hours.
In the aquarium, the algae must grow continuously, as these fish will eat practically only algae. The aquarium must have a volume of 60 liters for a small group of 10 Otocinclus.
With this information you can now add a small group of Otocinclus to your aquarium, making the walls clean and giving a good peaceful and tropical environment.
This fish has the name of pike because that is the name of the Polish weapon it resembles. It also has other common names such as the great northern pike, grass pike, the crocodile fish (this is because its head is similar to that of a crocodile).
In this type of species, the sex of each specimen has a great difference from the other. The males are sterile and cannot continue to have offspring, so they are a single generation species.
Not only do they use this great starter to hunt, but to avoid being involved in life-threatening situations. They may have a sedentary life, but when they detect their prey, They employ the blasts to launch and capture them without too much trouble.
They can be found in any habitat that have a body of water and have plenty of food for them. They require suitable places for spawning, as it is an essential element for their reproduction.
This is related to the dependence these fish have on the presence of vegetation to hide from others. Fewer plants grow in murky waters due to lack of light and strong water currents, so they will have trouble hiding from their own and hunting.
This is due to the fact that they guarantee reproductive success since more than half of the eggs will not reach adulthood. Once the eggs are released by the females, if the water temperature is less than six degrees, they will not hatch.
Fish Black Phantom Tetra, They are originally from the continent of South America, exactly from the areas of upper Paraguay. These little fish belong to the characid family and are also known by their scientific name Hyphessobrycon megalopterus.
Ghost Tetra fish can measure up to 7 centimeters in their natural habitat, but they barely reach 4 centimeters in captivity. In the same way, its body is divided into two areas in which the following colors are distinguished: on the back they are jet black, while on the previous one, they have two vertical bars of two different tones, one black and the other.
Keep in mind that the reproduction of these animals is very difficult, but possible, at least 50 liters of water are required. In the same way that reproduction occurs in other species, with this fish it can occur in pairs or with groups where male fish predominate.
Both seas and oceans are, without a doubt, one of the sources richest, in terms of biodiversity, on the planet Earth. Its interior houses countless guests who make them fascinating places.
They are distributed in well-lit spaces, ranging from the surface itself to 200 meters deep. This layer is known as phiotic zone.
They can be of the plant type (phytoplankton) or of the animal type (zooplankton). Unfortunately, these organisms, due to their anatomy, they can't beat the ocean currents, so they are dragged by them.
They are those living beings that have made the surface film of water their home.
If we focus on the group that make up the pelagic fish as such, we can make another subdivision, which lies, in the same way, depending on the aquatic areas that they populate:
Coastal pelagic organisms are usually small fish that live in large schools that move around the continental shelf and near the surface. An example of this are animals such as anchovies or sardines.
Within this group are the medium and large species that tend to migrate. All of them have characteristics, both anatomical and physiological, very similar to those of their coastal relatives, while their feeding patterns are different.
Since the term pelagic refers to a certain area of the sea and ocean, a word also arises that is used to mention it in its position as it is "abyssal". And therefore, in the same way that we refer to pelagic organisms and fish, we can also address them as fish or abyssal organisms.
Benthic organisms are those that coexist in the aquatic ecosystems background, unlike pelagic organisms.
Already immersed in the aphotic background, lacking light and located at great depths, there are consuming organisms, which depend on organic remains and microorganisms that gravity drags from the most superficial water levels to be able to feed themselves.
At first glance, it is not surprising that, after reading the above, we are very unfamiliar with benthic organisms. Nothing could be further from the truth.
As mentioned above, within the benthic organisms we find those types of fish classified as "peluronectiform", belonging to the order of fish flounder, roosters and sole. Related article:
