Today, there are still many picturesque animals that coexist with us in our seas, rivers, oceans, etc. Picturesque-looking, strange behaviors, etc., and very little known, that's how they are.
Its natural habitat corresponds to the depths of the oceans, reaching up to 4000 meters. This circumstance has made these animals a real enigma for science, since they are very difficult to study.
Its skin is covered by small scales that give it a brownish-gray color that can turn black. They do not have teeth, but plates that help them crush the shells of mollusks and crustaceans, which are the basis of their diet.
As a curiosity, it is the only vertebrate to show signs of a third pair of limbs.
The sunfish is one of the bony fish heaviest in the world, about a ton on average. Individuals have been found that reach 3 meters in length and 2000 kg.
Their diet consists mainly of zooplankton, which they consume in enormous quantities. Females can lay up to 300 million eggs, a figure that cannot be reached by any other vertebrate that we currently know.
Sloane's Viperfish is one of the most well-known and voracious predators of the deep seas and oceans.
Its main hallmark is its huge mouth, adorned with large fangs-like teeth that give it a diabolical appearance. Another of its characteristics is the long spine ending in a photophore (organ that emits light), which serves as a mechanism to attract prey.
They are fish that, in freedom and in their natural environment, can reach 30 years of life.
The drop fish is typical of the deep and temperate waters of the coasts of Australia and Tasmania, in a range of 600 and 1200 meters. It belongs to the family of scorpion fish.
The diet of this animal is very poor. It feeds on any edible matter that is suspended in water.
The red-lipped batfish inhabit the waters of the Galapagos Islands, about 30 meters deep. It belongs to the genus of Ogcocephalus fish.
Indeed, its head is very peculiar, since it has a structure called illicium, which it uses to attract its prey. It mainly feeds on small fish and crustaceans.
These types of fish are distributed throughout the oceans Pacific, Atlantic and Indian. It is also known as "Transparent head fish".
They are not very active animals, but they swim calmly in search of possible prey (crustaceans) with which to feed. Pacific ax fish
This animal has a very small body, about 8 cm, in proportion to its head, thin and flattened on the sides, which gives it the appearance of an ax. He has very large tube-shaped eyes, with which he looks up all the time.
His appearance is apparently evil. However, this fish is very calm and harmless.
