In this article we are going to talk about the characteristics of the immortal jellyfish and we will learn more about its secrets.
It has been found in seas around the world. Some studies have found the correlation between their locations after spotting them at various points and it has been found that they have genetics mixed with other species of jellyfish.
Life begins as a planula larva, like any other jellyfish of another species. When released to the sea, it will be able to feed until it can settle on a rock that it can use to supply itself with food.
If the jellyfish grows and in its adult phase there comes a time when a disease causes them enough damage that their life can end, they are able to reverse the entire process. Namely, they are able to break down the entire cellular system to form a polyp again and of those that will come out jellyfish that will be an exact copy of the adult.
Like other animals such as protozoa and other organisms such as sea sponges they breathe through cell diffusion. That is, they carry out a gas exchange with the dissolved oxygen in the water thanks to the activity of their own cells.
Today we want to share with you the characteristics of rainbow trout, A species of fish that usually inhabit the fresh water of western North America.
This pretty trout It is native to the lakes and rivers of the Rocky Mountain area (North America). Over the years the fish has been introduced throughout the world due to its use in sport fishing and its succulent meat.
The rainbow trout is a relative of the salmon family, and like these it can reach a significant size. Although the average reaches 76 centimeters, some specimens that measured more than 1.20 meters and weighed more than 24 kilos have been seen.
They feed on insects, crustaceans and smaller fish. Currently it is a species present, abundantly, throughout the world.
The eyes are smaller in size and are on the edge of the head. This makes it quite interesting, since by having your eyes in that place you can have different perspectives than other fish are used to.
Scientists affirm that the calluses of the skin act as a shield to protect against the bites of certain predators that are similar in size to their own. Obviously these hardnesses have nothing to do with some large predators such as the White shark.
As for their habitat, the best habitat where they can reproduce and live is near coral reefs. They usually use the crevices of the same or of rocks near them to hide at night and guarantee that they are not captured by predators.
At night they hide in some rock crevices and near corals to be able to escape from predators. Some species of triggerfish become very aggressive when they are in the breeding season because they are very territorial and defensive with their young.
As we have said before, some divers have been attacked and bitten by some specimens of female triggerfish. These females consider any individual in close proximity to be a threat to their young.
Its main food is to eat meats of different species such as shrimp, mollusks, worms, crabs and sea urchins. It is a carnivorous species that uses their fins to dig holes that help them get their food.
To catch their prey well they dig a deep hole for a few minutes to have more openness. It can often be observed how there are other species of fish that help triggerfish to take advantage of the food it provides and act as scavengers eating the leftovers.
I hope this information helps you to know more about triggerfish.
When it comes to knowing how many fish we can put in an aquarium, the type of tank influences. A wide and shallow one is recommended rather than a deep and narrow one, because the greater the surface of water exposed to the air, the greater the gas exchange with the water, there will be more oxygen and it will be able to house more fish.
Every fish needs its space. Overpopulation will give us many problems and between them it will be a continuous war because the problems between them will be constant: fights, nibbling of fins and cannibalism, and above all, problems with water, filtration and quality in the ecosystem.
The rule of one liter of water for each centimeter since they mainly refer to cichlids but it always works for us. If we want the aquarium planted with real plants or we have other types of fish such as koi carp and goldfish are you have to have more water as it is very dirty.
Therefore, if our aquarium has a large number of this type of fish, we will be able to house fewer individuals. As a summary, we can establish some main guidelines knowing the main conditions that determine how many fish we can put in the aquarium:
Size that they will have in adult: there are many species that grow too large compared to their size when they are small. One of the main mistakes newbies in this world make is not contemplating how tall pets are going to be when they reach adulthood.
Number of males and females: when introducing the fish into the aquarium, it is necessary to count how many males and how many females we introduce. This also has an impact on the rate of reproduction.
How many fish can be put in the tropical or cold water aquarium
This rule tells us that we can accommodate one centimeter of fish for every 12 cm² of surface. In such a way we can say that for cold water fish we have 62 square centimeters for each centimeter of fish.
