It is about the impressive flying fish. How is it possible that a fish, whose habitat is underwater, have the skills to plan outside of it?
2 Shape of your body and flight
These "wings" give them the ability of the fish to glide relatively easily out of the water. Its body also has a very dynamic morphology to which its pelvic fins are attached and make it a real flying fish.
They are also considered very intelligent animals, since they have been able to add these abilities throughout their evolution to increase their chances of survival in the ocean.
Thanks to the fact that they do not weigh much, they can glide longer in the air when they jump. They have the upper lobe of the tail fin of a medium size and on the edge of their body it has some folds that go to both sides.
When these fish take flight (again we clarify that it is not a flight as such, but more an activity of extreme gliding) it is quite a spectacle. When they glide, They are capable of traveling distances between 60 and 100 meters at a speed of 55 kilometers per hour.
Seeing a flying fish glide is fantastic, but seeing one of them perform these gliding maneuvers is a spectacle of nature. These fish are found most of the time doing these jumps and staying out of the water.
They are good at sheltering in places where they can easily get their food. The most common flying fish is established in the waters of the Atlantic and the Mediterranean.
The feeding of these fish is basically to eat plankton. On many occasions they can also eat other small fish and some of medium size.
When the eggs hatch, many larvae hatch and bear no resemblance to the characteristics of a flying fish. As they become adults, they acquire their special characteristics.
