The first World Championship was organized in 1991 and the following year a large field of competitors turned out for the first Youth World Championships in Basel, Switzerland in a clear sign of the growing popularity of the sport. By the end of the 1990’s, bouldering was officially introduced and together with lead and speed disciplines resulted in the creation of the World Cup.
Estimates put global participation in climbing sports around 35 million and climbing teams (the grass-roots breeding ground for future World Champions and Olympic hopefuls) can be found at most gyms. In the time since the first SportRoccia, climbing has evolved into a modern and professional athletic series that celebrates alpine culture and community with a global audience.
