1 What is the longest river in the world: the Nile or the Amazon?
3 Life on the Amazon River
In Africa we find the river Nilo, the most important in Africa and more specifically in Egypt, Tanzania, Sudan and Ethiopia, which is where its waters flow. It was the river that gave life to one of the most advanced civilizations of antiquity, that of ancient Egypt, and today it attracts many tourists and fans of the country's ancient history.
The Amazon, the longest river in the world
Apparently, it was believed that the river originated in the north of Peru instead of the south, until a group of scientists went on an expedition to Peru. It is now known that he wears a fifth of all river water on the planet, which makes it not only the longest river, but also the largest in the world.
At its widest point it can have up to 11 kilometers wide, and that in the dry season. In the wet season, the flooded area of the Amazon basin rises to 350.000 square kilometers.
Angel of the seagymnosomata): it is a transparent sea slug, without a shell. When swimming it moves appendages similar to angel wings, which are what gives it its name.
Hummingbird (Trochilinae): It is a typical bird of the American rainforests. It is very small, so much so that it barely weighs 2 grams.
Piracucu (Arapaima): it is the largest freshwater fish in the world. It can measure more than 3m long and weigh about 250kg.
Water fern (Azolla): It has oval leaves that are attached around the base. On the upper side of the leaves it has stiff hairs measuring 2,5cm.
Water lettuce (Pistia stratiotes): it is covered with fine hairs on the top and bottom of the outside of the plant. Its leaves are about 4cm long and float on the surface of the river.
