What is procrastination and why does it occur?
Sometimes they do it conscientiously and sometimes unconsciously. Procrastination or procrastination tends to happen much more often than you might imagine, and for many, it is synonymous with laziness or laziness.
They waste time, and when they waste too much, they try not to think about it and they keep wasting even more time.
For a behavior to be classified as procrastination or procrastination it must be counterproductive, unnecessary and taking too long. Planned actions are voluntarily delayed despite being emotionally worse for not doing them when they are due.
Trying to do something other than your responsibilities… This destructive spiral of putting off work is very difficult to escape.
People experience the effects of wasting time and missing deadlines, it is devastating both on a business and personal level.Procrastination or procrastination can end in stress, feelings of guilt and crisis, severe loss of personal productivity, as well as social and business disapproval for not meeting responsibilities or commitments. These feelings can escalate and create further procrastination… re-entering a dangerous downward spiral.
Sometimes chronic procrastination is a sign of an underlying psychological disorder. However, procrastination can also be seen as a useful way of identifying what is important to us personally, as it's rare to procrastinate when you really value the task at hand.
When it is postponed it happens because there is a break with people's self-control and they are more impulsive than it seems. You know what you have to do but you are not able to do it ...
The procrastinator has a high level of impulsive behavior and lacks self-control and discipline. They engage in some form of ego control and deny responsibility, making justifications (excuses) to delay what they should have done.
Self-confidence is essential to be able to be successful in life and this is where procrastinators find the greatest difficulty. It is important that people identify what is happening to them and are aware that immediate gratification is sometimes not always the best solution.
Changing people into lazy beasts. Why bother writing a few pages for a job, when we can try this cool new game on Facebook?
The problem is that we gain absolutely nothing by spending time on these simple pleasures. After a while, When we realize that we are almost out of time, we get to work.All we can handle is rushed work and just well done, and we are never satisfied with the results ...
Are you a person who procrastinates or who prefers to achieve goals first and rest later?
