History of the Number System | Culture 10
The base used in all civilizations was always the number 10, excluding the Babylonian numbering, which used a range between 10 and 60, unlike the Mayans who used a number system that ranged between 20 and 5. From 5,000 years ago, most civilizations have always counted in units, hundreds, thousands, and so on.
Most peoples who use a number system represent the whole numbers exactlyUnfortunately, many of them did not reach a certain amount and had to represent it with figures or hieroglyphs. Those who would finish perfecting our current number system would be the Hindus.
Thanks to the origin of the zero figure, there would no longer be gross errors when making figures such as 36, 360 or 3006 since In the past, empty spaces were used to distinguish these types of numbers that so many times caused abysmal errors for mathematicians.
Un foot it is a unit of length that, as its name implies, is based on the human foot. This is a measure that has been used by numerous civilizations ancient and that, among other things, was used to measure the stone blocks used for constructions.
The foot, as a unit of length, has been replaced in most countries of the world by units of the System International, except in some Anglo-Saxon countries where it is still maintained. It is still used in aeronautics to indicate the altitude.
1 How to go from feet to meters
Therefore, to convert feet en meters Only the following formula should be used: multiply the number of feet by 0,3048 and you will obtain the meters. An airplane flying for example at 20000 feet is 6096 meters above the ground.
In this case, we will leave the approximations to always be able to obtain the ideal answer. Only by learning a series of steps or formulas, we can answer the question of: How do you go from meters to feet?
In these two ways, you can already convert the amount you want, both in feet and square feet. Without a doubt, it is one of the fastest and easiest ways.
