What languages are spoken in Asia?
Thus, it is easy that several languages have emerged throughout its history. But, Do you know what languages are spoken in Asia?
1 Main languages of Asia
Main languages of Asia
We must also mention the Bengali which is the official language of Indonesia, although it is also spoken in other areas such as Bangladesh. There are a total of 189 million speakers of this language worldwide.
In turn, the Korean As you well know, it is used throughout North and South Korea, although it is also spoken in some areas of China, Japan, the United States, the Philippines and Russia. It is worth mentioning that statistics indicate that there are no less than 75 million speakers worldwide.
A language that is also widely used is Hindustani. A total of 474 million human beings in India and Pakistan have it as their mother tongue, but it must be said that it is also used in Fiji, Guyana, Malaysia and Suriname.
El Javanese It is another of the languages that we have to speak of, and never better said . With 75 million speakers from Indonesia, East Timor, Malaysia and Suriname, it ranks as the seventh most widely spoken language in all of Asia.
We must also mention the Persian language, which is spoken in Iran, Afghanistan and Tajikistan. Currently it is believed that there are 100 million people who speak this language.
El tamil It is another of the main languages used in the Asian continent. It is spoken by 63 million speakers in India and northwestern Sri Lanka.
Another of the most used languages in Asia is Turkish. Today there are 59 million human beings who use it daily.
Finally, we include the wu, which is a widely used language in the Asian continent, specifically China, where it comes from. 77 million human beings use this language in that country.
These are the most widely spoken languages in Asia by number of inhabitants, although they are not the only ones you will hear if you ever visit the continent. Other languages, such as Syriac, Aramaic, Thai, Burushaski or Nivkh are just a few that, although they are a minority, have given life to the culture and tradition of each of the places you can visit.
