One of the many things for which the Middle Ages –The historical period of Western civilization between the XNUMXth and XNUMXth centuries– were the enormous inequalities between nobles and peasants, or what is the same, between rich and poor.
The gentlemen they were to serve their lord in times of war. They enjoyed more freedoms and rights than the peasants, but their lives were always at risk, as battles during the Middle Ages occurred very frequently.
Unlike the peasants, who lived in humble one-room huts, the nobles lived in beautiful castles surrounded by servants and enough comforts, although not too many, since the purpose of these constructions was to provide the maximum possible protection to its inhabitants, so other aspects of the interior were often neglected, becoming humid, smelly and, above all, very cold.
