The importance of edible plants is fundamental for man, but also for most animal species since They are responsible for manufacturing the necessary oxygen so that we can breathe. Plants are mainly divided into three types based on their size: trees, shrubs, bushes, and herbaceous plants.
3 Edible plants for salads
The herb whose scientific name is Borago officinalisIt has large lanceolate-shaped leaves, and also good-sized flowers. All its parts can be consumed: the leaves in tortillas, the stems scrambled with mushrooms, and the flowers in salads.
Plantago is a herb that is very easy to recognize due to the longitudinal veins it has on the leaves. It can be between 3 and 7, which is why it is often called 'rib weed'.
Basil, known by the scientific name of Ocimum basilicum, it is an herb that is used for prevent and treat poor appetite, cuts and skin wounds, for example, in salads. You see removing the youngest leaves from time to time, to take advantage of their benefits.
Parsley, or Petroselinum crispum, is a perennial herb that helps you prevent halitosis (bad breath) and flatulence. In addition, you can use it in different dishes, as a condiment in white meats, salads, sauces ...
Rosemary is a subshrub whose scientific name is Rosmarinus officinalis. It is one of the most interesting medicinal plants, since helps to focus, purify the bodyAs regulate blood pressure.
Salvia is an herb that, in addition to being very beautiful to produce small but decorative flowers, is an edible plant. It can be used as a condiment in different dishes, since its leaves have a very pleasant taste.
But not only do people eat plants, but also the animals that live in our environment also eat them, but usually they are not the same. Some edible plants do not reward us with a fruit, but are used to flavor foods or use the leaves for infusions.
The grain of cereals is found inside a cellulose shell, which in turn is also used in diets. In recent years it seems that declared a war on gluten, components that we can also find in some types of cereals.
Fruit has always been associated with dessert, the last dish of meals, although it can also be eaten sporadically between meals. It can be eaten raw or well cooked, although we can also find it in the form of jam or juices.
The animal cell is said to be a type of eukaryotic cell, that is, those with a well-organized cell nucleus. Furthermore, it is enveloped by the so-called nuclear envelope and many other parts.
1 What is the animal cell
Broadly speaking we can define animal cell as a unit or type of eukaryotic cell, which is vital for the animals or beings of 'Animalia'. This type of cells will be in charge of carrying out processes such as producing energy or the proper functioning of metabolism.
It should be mentioned that the fundamental parts of the animal cell They are three main: the envelope of the cell, the cytoplasm and its nucleus. Although within some of these parts, we find cellular organelles or structures that should also be mentioned, since they are still vital parts of said cell.
El Lysosome It is a kind of sac that is responsible for the so-called 'cellular digestion'. That is, of the processes or reactions that occur in a cell.
Undoubtedly, the nucleus is another of the most important parts of every cell, both vegetables and animals. It is spherical and within it both DNA molecules and proteins are organized into chromosomes.
Chromatin is the set of DNA as well as the proteins that are found in the part of the nucleus of the cells and that constitute the genome of the cells.
Epithelial: They are responsible for covering the outside, both of the body and organs.
There is a type of meteorological phenomenon that is really very abundant in some areas of the world and can cause accidents since it makes visibility difficult. It's about the mist.
Keep reading if you want to know more.
3 Where is it most common?
5 Precautions to consider
Just like rain droplets form, fog needs small solid particles to condense on them and form. Therefore, we can easily find fog on the beach in the mornings, since the air is colder and the salt in the air in suspension serves as a condensation nucleus so that water vapor can form water droplets.
Where is it most common?
It is especially in autumn when the most intense fogs take place since the water on the surfaces still maintains the heat of summer. The water vapor that exists around the lakes and seas joins the cold air masses of autumn nights and condenses to form fog.
Another action commonly taken after entering a fog bank is to use high-beam headlights. This is a counterproductive action, since the amount of water droplets in the air, when they come into contact with light, will cause an important reflection that will trigger a glare that will make vision difficult even more.
To avoid condensation of water droplets on the windshield, we must have The windshield wipers in perfect condition.
Patience is the best ally in these situations. Keep in mind that you lose the notion of distance and places when driving through fog.
