The life cycle of a product is defined as the set of different stages that a product goes through on the market. The constant evolution and development of new technologies, fashions, eras, and even legislation determine the useful and limited life of the products that companies offer.
1.5 Decline stage, termination
2 Are the life cycles of products always the same?
4 Can you decide the best time to relaunch a product?
