They are called concession connectors but are also known as concessive connectors. Again they join words or phrases with the intention to indicate a difficulty, but this does not prevent the action from being carried out.
We will go to the beach by more than be cloudy.
Connectors: Because, because of, because, because of, because, because, because of, as a consequence.
Did because he felt like it.
He approved the driving license, as performed good maneuvers.
The same word already tells us what consequence connectors are. They try to show us the effect or consequence of what we are exposing through sentences.
As You can't accompany me, I'll go alone
I'll lend you the money as long as you return it to me every month.
In this case, when we talk about additive connectors, we have to say that they are the ones that will provide new and relevant information. A perfect way to introduce new data in the sentence.
You arrive without warning and, to top, with five friends.
He was her tutor, that is, your responsible.
The situation has not changed, rather, has not improved.
In this case, thanks to the temporary connectors, we will be able to know when the action described in the phrases happened. Of course, the temporals can be divided into connectors of anteriority, simultaneity and posteriority.
