Separate the roots by the sign that corresponds to the second term
The coefficient of the first term must be 1.
The second term has the same letter as the first term, but it is not squared, that is, it has an exponent of 1.
The third term has nothing to do with the first, nor with the second term. In other words, it is a question of any quantity, without any relation to the previous ones.
The first term of both binomials must be the square root of the first term of the trinomial, that is: "x".
If the second term and the third term have a positive sign, both binomials will have a positive sign.
If the second term is positive and the third is negative, the two terms will have different signs. The positive sign will be assigned to the number with the highest absolute value.
